## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

This is a textbook **"coverage-touching" test suite** — every production method is invoked (giving you line coverage) but almost nothing is actually verified. These tests will pass even if the code is completely broken.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Assertion-Free Tests (No Verification)

| # | Test | Problem |
|---|------|---------|
| 1 | `AddProduct_Works` | Zero assertions. Would pass even if `Save()` threw silently or did nothing. |
| 2 | `UpdatePrice_Works` | Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the product's price changed. |
| 3 | `RemoveProduct_Works` | Calls `RemoveProduct` but never verifies the product is gone. |
| 4 | `GetProductCount_Works` | Captures `count` into a variable and discards it — no assert at all. |
| 5 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | Applies a 10% discount to two products but never checks any price. |
| 6 | `ImportFromCsv_Works` | Imports a product but never verifies it was stored. |

**Fix pattern:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);
    var stored = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(product, stored);
}

[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
}

[TestMethod]
public void RemoveProduct_DeletesProduct()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
}

[TestMethod]
public void ApplyBulkDiscount_ReducesPrices()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 100m));
    _catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
    Assert.AreEqual(90m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
}
```

---

### 🟠 HIGH — Shallow / Trivial Assertions

| # | Test | Problem |
|---|------|---------|
| 7 | `GetProduct_Works` | Asserts `IsNotNull` but never checks `Sku`, `Name`, or `Price`. A bug returning the wrong product passes. |
| 8 | `SearchProducts_Works` | Asserts `IsNotNull` on the list but never checks count or contents. Would pass if search returned zero results or the wrong products. |
| 9 | `GetAllProducts_Works` | Same — `IsNotNull` on a list that is always non-null (even if empty). |
| 10 | `ExportToCsv_Works` | `IsNotNull` on a string — even `""` would pass. |

**Fix pattern:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetProduct_ReturnsCorrectProduct()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    var result = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001", result!.Sku);
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", result.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, result.Price);
}

[TestMethod]
public void Search_FiltersCorrectly()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-002", "Gadget", 19.99m));
    var results = _catalog.Search("Widget");
    Assert.AreEqual(1, results.Count);
    Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001", results[0].Sku);
}

[TestMethod]
public void ExportToCsv_FormatsCorrectly()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    var csv = _catalog.ExportToCsv();
    Assert.AreEqual("SKU-001,Widget,9.99", csv);
}
